#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:4
msgid "Booting guest operating systems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:6
msgid ""
"Hexagon VM guests require a Hexagon VM host. QEMU ships board-specific host "
"firmware in ``pc-bios``. Guest operating systems boot with the "
"``hexagon_loadlinux_*`` images; the ``hexagon_booter_*`` images run H2 user "
"programs instead (see :doc:`cdsp`). Select a matching machine, firmware, and "
"guest memory layout from :doc:`cdsp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:13
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:15
msgid ""
"The kernel must be built for the Hexagon VM interface and include the PL011 "
"console and required virtio-mmio device drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:18
msgid "For a preloaded kernel and separate initramfs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:20
msgid ""
"qemu-system-hexagon -M qcs6490-cdsp -display none -serial stdio \\\n"
"    -bios hexagon_loadlinux_qcs6490_cdsp \\\n"
"    -kernel ./vmlinux -initrd ./initramfs.cpio.gz \\\n"
"    -append \"console=ttyAMA0 rdinit=/init\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:27
msgid ""
"``ttyAMA0`` selects the PL011 console. ``-append`` sets the boot arguments "
"in QEMU's DTB; the guest and its VM host determine how those arguments are "
"consumed. Add any platform-specific memory or delay-calibration parameters "
"required by the kernel image."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:33
msgid "Guest operating systems on virt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:35
msgid ""
"The ``virt`` machine boots a guest operating system through the same "
"firmware:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:38
msgid ""
"qemu-system-hexagon -M virt -display none -serial stdio \\\n"
"    -bios hexagon_loadlinux_sa8775p_cdsp \\\n"
"    -kernel ./guest.elf -append \"console=ttyAMA0\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../system/hexagon/operating-systems.rst:44
msgid ""
"QEMU loads the guest ELF at its declared physical addresses. QEMU enters the "
"firmware with the DTB address in ``r1:r0`` (see :ref:`hexagon-vm-boot`). The "
"guest must use the Hexagon VM interface for interrupts and timers, the PL011 "
"at ``0x10000000``, and the virtio-mmio transports listed in :doc:`machines`."
msgstr ""
